    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 13 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Each player aims to take exactly the number of tricks they bid in the second phase. Score 10 plus the square of tricks for exact bid; lose 10 per trick over or under. Zero bid has special scoring. First to reach agreed target score wins.',
      "Turn-flow example: Two-phase bidding: first phase (dealer starts, clockwise) bids 5-13 tricks plus suit or no trumps (Bridge order: no trumps highest, then spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). After four consecutive passes, last bidder is declarer and trump is set. Second phase: other three players (declarer's left clockwise) each bid number of tricks (0+); fourth player cannot bid so total equals 13. Game is over if total>13, under if <13. Declarer leads; must follow suit; highest trump wins trick else highest of led suit. Winner of trick leads next. After 13 tricks, score each player.",
      'Scoring example: Exact bid: 10 plus square of tricks; off by N tricks: minus 10N. Zero bid: fail -50 for first trick then +10 each; zero made under 50, over 30. Cumulative total; game ends when one reaches agreed target; highest wins; tie broken by further hands. First player to reach or exceed the agreed target score wins. Tie: play further hands until one player has highest total..',
